    "Stem": "Ridgeway Manufacturing operates 14 plants across six countries and maintains a centralized internal audit function of four professionals. The current-year internal audit plan allocates 65% of audit hours to financial reporting controls, 25% to operational audits, and 10% to compliance. Ridgeway's external auditor noted in last year's management letter that the company's fraud risk assessment had not been updated in three years, despite the opening of four new plants in jurisdictions with Transparency International Corruption Perception Index scores below 35. The CFO proposes outsourcing the fraud risk assessment to the external audit firm's advisory practice, arguing that the four-person internal audit team lacks bandwidth. The audit committee chair counters that COSO requires management — not external consultants — to own the fraud risk assessment. Under COSO Principle 9, which of the following represents the most appropriate evaluation of Ridgeway's fraud risk assessment situation?",
